      "target": "../sections/sec-014-alternate-notation-for-some-conformance-requirem.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This standard contains more than a few cardinality assertions, each of which indicates the minimum and maximum number of\ntimes a property may appear. These are represented by using “minCount” and “maxCount” respectively. The absolute minimum\nnumber of occurrences is zero (0), while for an unbounded maximum number of occurrences a star (*) is being used.\nHere are some examples:\n• minCount: 1\n• maxCount: *\n• Cardinality: 0..1\n• Cardinality: 0..*\n• Cardinality: 1..1\n• Cardinality: 1..*\nEach of these assertions can easily be understood as to whether a feature is required, and if so, how many occur",
