      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Core Profile compliance point",
      "pageStart": 16,
      "pageEnd": 17,
      "target": "../sections/sec-016-core-profile-compliance-point.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The Core Profile includes the definitions of classes properties and vocabularies usable by all SPDX profiles when producing or\nconsuming SPDX content. Although the classes, properties and vocabularies are somewhat extensive, the required fields are\nrather minimal to allow maximum flexibility while meeting minimum SBOM requirements. Software that conforms to the SPDX\nspecification at the Core Profile compliance point shall be able to import and export serialized documents that conform with one\nof the defined SPDX serialization formats.\nConformance to the Core Profile compliance point is mandato",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/omg-2024-spdx-3-0/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Software Profile compliance point",
      "pageStart": 17,
      "pageEnd": 17,
      "target": "../sections/sec-017-software-profile-compliance-point.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The Software Profile includes the definitions of classes, properties and vocabularies for referring to and conveying information\nabout software and is usable by all SPDX profiles when producing or consuming SPDX content.\nSoftware that conforms to the SPDX specification at the Software Profile compliance point shall be able to import and export\nserialized documents that conform with one of the SPDX serialization formats defined SPDX serialization formats.\nConformance to the Software Profile compliance point does not entail support for the Licensing, Dataset, AI, Build, Lite, or\nExtension profil",
