      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Case sensitivity",
      "pageStart": 186,
      "pageEnd": 186,
      "target": "../sections/sec-328-case-sensitivity.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "License expression operators (AND, and, OR, or, WITH and with) should be matched in a case-sensitive manner, i.e., letters\nmust be all upper case or all lower case.\nLicense identifiers (including license exception identifiers) used in SPDX documents or source code files should be matched in a\ncase-insensitive manner. In other words, MIT, Mit and mIt should all be treated as the same identifier and referring to the same\nlicense.\nHowever, please be aware that it is often important to match with the case of the canonical identifier on the SPDX License List3.\nThis is because the canonical identifi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
