    {
      "id": "library/omg-2024-spdx-3-0/blocks/prose-sec-397",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "History with OMG, Motivation and Rational (Informative)",
      "pageStart": 204,
      "pageEnd": 208,
      "target": "../sections/sec-397-history-with-omg-motivation-and-rational-informa.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The OMG and CISQ involvement in developing this specification had its start due to a need that came from the several years of work\nin the Department of Commerce’s National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA) in creating an Initiative\nto Improve Software Component Transparency in July of 2018 [6]. That effort actually was the culmination of several earlier\nattempts to get software transparency, updatability and bill of materials as requirements in safety critical sectors like automotive\nand healthcare as early as 2013/2014 [2, 3] with many talks and papers written for and a",
